Package: GradBoostR
Type: Package
Title: Gradient Boosting, Random Forests, and Neural Networks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
        given = "Nic",
        family = "Coxen",
        email = "nicjcoxen@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
    )
Description: Provides implementations of machine-learning methods related to
    gradient boosting, random forests, neural network regression, decision
    stumps, and binary random forest classification. Background for gradient
    boosting is provided by Friedman (2001)
    <doi:10.1214/aos/1013203451>, while random forests are described by
    Breiman (2001) <doi:10.1023/A:1010933404324>. The neural network
    functionality uses a multilayer feedforward architecture; theoretical
    background for this class of networks is provided by Hornik, Stinchcombe,
    and White (1989) <doi:10.1016/0893-6080(89)90020-8>. Native code
    integration uses 'Rcpp' as described by Eddelbuettel and Francois (2011)
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v040.i08> and 'RcppArmadillo' as described by
    Eddelbuettel and Sanderson (2014)
    <doi:10.1016/j.csda.2013.02.005>. The package provides a unified modelling
    interface, prediction functions, cross-validation examples, and native
    implementations using 'Rcpp' and 'RcppArmadillo'.
